    "placement": "From the last mark on the displayed course, boats shall sail to the finish line passing the Spit mark to starboard. The finishing line, unless a race is shortened, shall be in the vicinity of the Spit Mark (S) and the South Rowan Buoy (R) and shall be between a spherical orange Mark F and the main mast (or red/white pole) on the adjacent Committee Finishing Vessel displaying a blue flag.",
